            <ArticleTitle>Effects of a long-term transfusion regimen on sickle cell-related illnesses.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>909-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The efficacy of a long-term transfusion regimen in preventing sickle cell disease complications is unknown. We examined 17 patients before, during, and after transfusion for cerebral vascular accident and vaso-occlusive crisis. Total hospitalization rate, as well as admissions for vaso-occlusive crisis, cases of acute chest syndrome, and bacterial infections decreased while patients were on a transfusion regimen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
